Package: FlowerTrait
Type: Package
Title: Colour, Pattern, Symmetry and Shape Traits of Flowers from Photographs
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ehsan", "Rahimi", email = "ehsanrahimi666@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-8401-472X")),
    person("Chuleui", "Jung", email = "cjung@gknu.ac.kr", role = "aut"))
Description: Extracts colour, pattern, symmetry and shape traits of flowers
    from field photographs: single photos, folders of photos, folders sorted
    by species, or photos of flowering observations found through the Global
    Biodiversity Information Facility ('GBIF') and 'iNaturalist'. An optional
    'Python' back end finds the main flower with 'Grounding DINO' in two
    passes, outlines it with 'Segment Anything' 2.1, screens each photo with a
    photo filter (usable photo, face view, open flower, whole flower, sharp)
    and computes the full trait set. Core colour traits, human colour names,
    centre-periphery colour contrast, radial and bilateral symmetry, petal
    number and outline quality metrics are also computed natively in R.
    Further functions convert reflectance spectra to the same colour space,
    apply decision rules, check colour casts and exposure, correct white
    balance, test trait stability under camera changes and image
    augmentation, estimate photo-to-photo repeatability and invariance, and
    report a catalogue of trait reliability. The methods were validated on
    photographs of angiosperm flowers from six continents against manual
    outlines and spectrophotometric measurements.
